{
  "models_id": "basic_models",
  "display_name": "Ultra-basic models: every aircraft, vehicle, site and building as a few primitives",
  "status": "First pass, 18 October 2026; the order of battle's equipment and our own aircraft added 22 October 2026 (the nation on the map, N3). Placeholders until real models exist: the right size, a recognisable silhouette, a colour per side (ours own_grey and own_camo, never the enemy's model of the same type).",
  "source": "game value: placeholders built from primitives; overall length, span and height are approximate public dimensions of each type, for scale only (presentation data, like data/cabins/)",
  "confidence": "estimate",
  "notes": "Each model is an archetype with a few parameters; simcore/scenery/basic_models.hpp expands it into parts (box, cylinder, cone, sphere) in the model's frame: x forward, y right, z up, metres, the origin on the ground under the middle (aircraft: at the middle of the fuselage). Archetypes: jet (length, span, height, engines, wing swept/delta/straight/variable, tail conventional/twin/none), prop (biplane, high_wing, engines 2: on the wings), helicopter (rotor_m, wings), drone, missile (diameter_m), wheeled (axles, turret, gun and barrels, radar dish/bar/none with the dish's diameter_m or the bar's span_m and antenna_h_m, missiles, mast, cab), tracked (the same), truck (body cargo/tank/box, missiles lying on a low bed with missile_m and diameter_m, a bar radar), radar (a post's cabin, the antenna span_m wide and antenna_h_m tall on its post), launcher (rails, missile_m, elevation_deg), gun (barrels), building (roof pitched/flat), church, tower (diameter_m: chimneys, cooling towers, tanks), tent, mast, tree (crown cone/round), bridge, crates. Colours are names from 'colours' or #rrggbb. The aircraft models carry the air war's aircraft ids (data/air_war/faction_*.json), and every equipment type of our order of battle (data/command/oob_pannonia.json) is a model: test_scenery checks both.",
